<suitelet scriptid="customscript_mcgi_sl_arch_split_execute">
  <description>CWP ARCH bundle split write path. Posts the Inventory Adjustment that splits a lot and trues the Sales Order line up to the measured quantities. Runs as Administrator because warehouse and trader roles cannot write inventory adjustments; authorisation is therefore enforced in script against custscript_arch_split_roles, which fails closed to Administrator only when unset.</description>
  <isinactive>F</isinactive>
  <name>MCGI SL ARCH Split Execute</name>
  <!-- admins=F matches every other script in this account. This endpoint is hit
       by warehouse staff, and it already handles expected refusals itself,
       returning JSON and logging them at AUDIT. Emailing all administrators
       on top of that is noise, and noise is how real failures get ignored.
       The owner still gets notified. -->
  <notifyadmins>F</notifyadmins>
  <notifyemails></notifyemails>
  <notifyowner>T</notifyowner>
  <notifyuser>F</notifyuser>
  <scriptfile>[/SuiteScripts/mcgi_services/trader_screen/entry_points/sl/mcgi_sl_arch_split_execute.js]</scriptfile>
  <scriptcustomfields>
    <scriptcustomfield scriptid="custscript_arch_split_roles">
      <accesslevel>2</accesslevel>
      <applyformatting>F</applyformatting>
      <checkspelling>F</checkspelling>
      <defaultchecked>F</defaultchecked>
      <defaultselection></defaultselection>
      <defaultvalue></defaultvalue>
      <description>Comma separated role internal IDs permitted to complete a bundle split. Leave EMPTY until the warehouse role is settled with the client: empty means Administrator only, which is the safe default for a deployment that writes as Administrator. Administrator is always retained even if omitted from the list, so a bad entry cannot lock out the person who has to fix it.</description>
      <displayheight></displayheight>
      <displaytype>NORMAL</displaytype>
      <displaywidth></displaywidth>
      <dynamicdefault></dynamicdefault>
      <fieldtype>TEXT</fieldtype>
      <help>Example: 1057,1063. Empty is safe and means Administrator only.</help>
      <isformula>F</isformula>
      <ismandatory>F</ismandatory>
      <label>Permitted Split Roles</label>
      <linktext></linktext>
      <maxlength></maxlength>
      <maxvalue></maxvalue>
      <minvalue></minvalue>
      <onparentdelete></onparentdelete>
      <searchlevel>2</searchlevel>
      <selectrecordtype></selectrecordtype>
      <setting></setting>
      <storevalue>T</storevalue>
    </scriptcustomfield>
  </scriptcustomfields>
  <scriptdeployments>
    <scriptdeployment scriptid="customdeploy_mcgi_sl_arch_split_execute">
      <allemployees>F</allemployees>
      <allpartners>F</allpartners>
      <allroles>F</allroles>
      <!-- Administrator only, until the warehouse role is settled with the client.
           allemployees=F is not by itself enough: an admin does NOT bypass a
           Suitelet audience, so with no role listed the endpoint refuses
           everyone including the person who has to test it. Add the warehouse
           role HERE as well as to custscript_arch_split_roles when it is known;
           the audience decides who can reach the URL, the parameter decides who
           the script will act for. -->
      <audslctrole>ADMINISTRATOR</audslctrole>
      <eventtype></eventtype>
      <isdeployed>T</isdeployed>
      <isonline>F</isonline>
      <loglevel>DEBUG</loglevel>
      <runasrole>ADMINISTRATOR</runasrole>
      <status>RELEASED</status>
      <title>MCGI SL ARCH Split Execute</title>
    </scriptdeployment>
  </scriptdeployments>
</suitelet>
